 ## Overview
-Classical Dual Contouring with Estimated Normals (DC-est) is a surface extraction method that generates a mesh from a Signed Distance Field (SDF) by placing a single vertex inside each grid cell intersected by the isosurface, determined by minimizing a Quadratic Error Function (QEF) [S1]. It differs from its siblings by relying on analytically estimated surface normals derived from local SDF gradients rather than ray-intersected normals or learned features [S1]. While it produces results comparable to or slightly better than Marching Cubes 33 (MC33) in Chamfer Distance (CD) and F1 scores, it is not expected to yield accurate normal estimates near sharp features [S1].
