 ## Background
-Classical Dual Contouring with Estimated Normals (DC-est) is a traditional method for isosurface extraction from Signed Distance Fields. It was evaluated in comparative studies against modern neural methods like Neural Dual Contouring (NDC) and Neural Marching Cubes (NMC) [S1]. The method relies on the classical dual contouring framework where vertex positions are determined by minimizing a QEF based on surface normals [S1]. The boundary cap variant was introduced in the Fracturing Fog project to address the lack of watertightness in standard DC implementations [S2, unofficial].
